      "id": "claim_a9e6fe40175741c3b29e742f045eb22e",
      "statement": "sidebar-tree.ts's governing rule is that the sidebar draws exactly one tree whose shape is decided by data alone; user action changes only sibling ordering under the same parent and collapse state, never the tree's shape. Three invariants it fixes: a child always lands under a root ancestor from the same project; no node crosses a container for any reason other than a color filter; and every linear ordering the UI needs (multi-pane slot order, swipe order) is derived from one depth-first traversal of that same tree.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://web/src/app/sidebar-tree.ts#L1-L21",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e607b02534b45939dc16b0409d22511f5628a6ea2d6b150687ceae42fcb74f8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
